    "summary": "Root cause: the accepted lane.xi was wrong. The lateral lane-load factor had been set to 0.78, which is the JTG D60-2015 Table 4.3.1-5 value for 3 design lanes, but this bridge has two design lanes (two-way, 9 m carriageway), for which xi = 1.0. The L2-1 provenance/recomputation check therefore failed the model. I re-proposed lane.xi = 1.0 citing JTGD60-4.3.1-xi and the instance's 2-lane data; the change is a code-load parameter only, so the structural decisions and modal results were unaffected.\n\nModel summary — Single simply supported span, 30 m bearing-to-bearing, 10 m deck (9 m carriageway, two-way, 2 design lanes). Spine-beam 2D idealization; 3 precast prestressed small-box C40 girders lumped to a single beam: A_single = 1.13893 m², I_single = 0.35492 m⁴, A = 3.41679 m², I = 1.06475 m⁴, Ec = 32500 MPa, γ = 26 kN/m³, w = 88.84 kN/m, m = 9.056 t/m. Both abutments carry plain laminated elastomeric bearings (300×400 mm, 5×8 mm rubber layers), 2 per girder end (6 per line): S = 10.714, Kv = 8.518e3 kN/m per line, Kh = 1.8e4 kN/m per line, vertical spring / longitudinal spring / rotation free at each line. Live load: Class II, qk = 7.875 kN/m, Pk = 240 kN, xi = 1.0, and impact factor μ = 0.2006 from f1.\n\nResults (all checks pass): first three vertical frequencies 3.402, 13.49, 29.88 Hz (f1 = 3.40 Hz, used for μ = 0.1767·ln f1 − 0.0157 = 0.2006); self-weight support reactions 1332.55 + 1332.55 = 2665.09 kN matching total girder self-weight; self-weight midspan moment 9994.10 kN·m; lane-load max positive moment at midspan 6449.63 kN·m."
